\title{Range of a function}
\date{2026-03-09T11:28:01Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\taxon{Definition}
\p{The \em{range} of a function #{f : A \to B} is the set ##{\{ b \in
    B \mid \exists a \in A \st f(a) = b \},} that is, the subset of #{B} consisting of all those #{b}’s which are actually the image of (at least one) #{a \in A}.}
